        "original_id": "ffe9e9d5-b225-58e3-b231-0bba89da7ea2",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Home Rule League, Irish Parliamentary Party\n- Concepts: Irish Home Rule movement, home rule for Ireland\n- People: John Dunbar\n- Roles: Member of Parliament for New Ross\n\nFacts:\n- The Irish Home Rule movement agitated for self-government for Ireland within the United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland.\n- The Home Rule League existed from 1873 to 1882 and campaigned for home rule for Ireland within the United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland.\n- The Home Rule League was also called the Home Rule Party or the Home Rule Confederation.\n- The Home Rule League was replaced by the Irish Parliamentary Party.\n- John Dunbar was a Home Rule League politician.\n- John Dunbar served as the Member of Parliament for New Ross from February 1874 until his death in 1878.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
