        "text": "Page: Home Rule League. Sentence: The Home Rule League (1873–1882), sometimes called the Home Rule Party or the Home Rule Confederation, was a political party which campaigned for home rule for Ireland within the United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland, until it was replaced by the Irish Parliamentary Party.\nPage: Irish Home Rule movement. Sentence: The Irish Home Rule movement was a movement that agitated for self-government for Ireland within the United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland.\nPage: John Dunbar (MP). Sentence: John Dunbar was a Home Rule League politician who served as the Member of Parliament for New Ross from February 1874 through to his death in 1878.",
